<title>USA: Pratt wins $170 mln Air China contract.</title>
<headline>Pratt wins $170 mln Air China contract.</headline>
<dateline>EAST HARTFORD, Conn. 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jet engine maker Pratt &amp; Whitney, a unit of United Technologies Corp, said Wednesday it won an engine contract from Air China worth about $170 million.</p>
<p>Pratt said the airline will use PW4000 family engines to power five Boeing Co 777 aircraft.</p>
<p>Air China will purchase 10 installed and three spare engines for the five aircraft, Pratt said in a statement.</p>
<p>Deliveries will begin in October 1998.  Pratt said it has more than a 40 percent market share for 777 aircraft engines.</p>
<p>((--Hartford newsroom, (860) 727-0224))</p>
